Chapter: SheetCellStoreTest
  cites Sheets chapter CellStore
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The dense cell store: a cell reads back what was set, an unset cell reads
 zero, a cell beyond the bounds is refused and reads zero, and a column and a
 row sum over a 1,000-row sheet answer the arithmetic. The sabotage: make
 sheet-off forget the header and "corner" reads the row count back; make
 sheet-in accept a column equal to the count and "beyond refused" turns no.

 Beside the numbers, the KIND and the text arena. The reading that says the
 tag is worth its four bytes is `zero is not empty`: a cell holding zero and
 a cell never written answer the same number and must not answer the same
 kind. The reading that says the tag is CONSUMED rather than merely stored is
 the column sum, which drops by exactly the number a text cell replaced
 rather than gaining that cell's arena offset.

 A text is graded by round trip and by arena arithmetic together, because a
 round trip alone passes for a store that hands back the last string written
 whatever cell is asked.

 The line asking whether a text cell reads as a number asks about cell 1,2
 and not 0,2. The FIRST text written sits at arena offset zero, so a
 `sheet-get` that ignored the kind entirely would answer 0 there, which is
 the same answer the correct code gives: that pair cannot tell the two apart.
 Sabotaging `sheet-get` to drop its kind test moves this line and the column
 sum, and nothing else.

Section: Body

  cs-yn : Boolean -> Text
  cs-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  cs-fill : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  cs-fill (blk) (r) =
    if r >= 1000 then 0
    else let s = sheet-set blk r 1 (r + 1)
    in cs-fill blk (r + 1)

  cs-kind-name : Integer -> Text
  cs-kind-name (k) = if k == 0 then "empty" else if k == 1 then "number" else "text"

 TWO sheets, because one cannot see the fault this line exists to catch.
 `sheet-arena` returned an OFFSET rather than an address, which named the
 same absolute region for every sheet in the program; a single sheet read
 back whatever it had written and passed, while the second sheet's first
 string overwrote the first sheet's.

  cs-two-sheets : Text
  cs-two-sheets =
    let a = sheet-new 4 4 64
    in let b = sheet-new 4 4 64
    in let wa = sheet-set-text a 0 0 "first"
    in let wb = sheet-set-text b 0 0 "second"
    in "a holds " & sheet-text a 0 0 & ", b holds " & sheet-text b 0 0 & ", both wrote at offset " & show (sheet-text-used a) & " and " & show (sheet-text-used b) & ", and the arenas differ " & (if sheet-arena a /= sheet-arena b then "yes" else "no")

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let blk = sheet-new 1000 26 256
    in let f = cs-fill blk 0
    in let s1 = sheet-set blk 0 0 7
    in let s2 = sheet-set blk 999 25 9
    in let beyond = sheet-set blk 1000 0 1
    in let beyond2 = sheet-set blk 0 26 1
    in let zero = sheet-set blk 3 3 0
    in let sum-before = sheet-col-sum blk 1
    in act
      print-line-uni ("bounds " & show (sheet-rows blk) & "x" & show (sheet-cols blk) & "  corner " & show (sheet-get blk 0 0) & " " & show (sheet-get blk 999 25) & "  unset " & show (sheet-get blk 500 3) & "  beyond refused " & cs-yn (beyond == False & beyond2 == False) & "  beyond reads " & show (sheet-get blk 1000 0))
      print-line-uni ("column 1 sum " & show sum-before & "  row 0 sum " & show (sheet-row-sum blk 0) & "  row 999 sum " & show (sheet-row-sum blk 999))
      print-line-uni ("zero is not empty: cell 3,3 reads " & show (sheet-get blk 3 3) & " and is " & cs-kind-name (sheet-kind blk 3 3) & ", cell 4,4 reads " & show (sheet-get blk 4 4) & " and is " & cs-kind-name (sheet-kind blk 4 4))
      print-line-uni ("a text round trips: set " & cs-yn (sheet-set-text blk 0 2 "Widgets") & "  reads " & sheet-text blk 0 2 & "  kind " & cs-kind-name (sheet-kind blk 0 2) & "  arena used " & show (sheet-text-used blk))
      print-line-uni ("a second text does not disturb the first: set " & cs-yn (sheet-set-text blk 1 2 "Cost per unit") & "  first " & sheet-text blk 0 2 & "  second " & sheet-text blk 1 2 & "  arena used " & show (sheet-text-used blk))
      print-line-uni ("a number cell has no text: " & cs-yn (sheet-text blk 0 0 == "") & "  and a text cell is not a number: cell 1,2 reads " & show (sheet-get blk 1 2))
      print-line-uni ("a text in a column of quantities is not summed: was " & show sum-before & "  set row 500 to a label " & cs-yn (sheet-set-text blk 500 1 "subtotal") & "  now " & show (sheet-col-sum blk 1) & "  dropped by " & show (sum-before - sheet-col-sum blk 1))
      print-line-uni ("clearing gives back the empty kind: " & cs-yn (sheet-clear blk 0 0) & " cell 0,0 is " & cs-kind-name (sheet-kind blk 0 0) & " reading " & show (sheet-get blk 0 0))
      print-line-uni ("the arena refuses rather than truncating: free " & show (sheet-text-free blk) & "  a string past it " & cs-yn (sheet-set-text blk 9 9 "0123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789") & "  cell 9,9 is " & cs-kind-name (sheet-kind blk 9 9) & "  arena used " & show (sheet-text-used blk))
      print-line-uni ("two sheets do not share an arena: " & cs-two-sheets)
    end
